2186123074 1078 #edb/ref 17592186432001 13194139534670 17592186045417 true] [17592186124333 1071 "![](images/36/36280c9a2392e04a68646d40908f6041a28017e63d6f8d96b25b518428cb9717.png)\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a basis of the eigenspace corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda=-4.$" 13194139534670 17592186045417 false] [17592186124333 1071 "![](images/5e/5ef5d9de719614493e56813f81386090eaf2329bc660ed8b4c1972080e1662f3.svg)\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a basis of the eigenspace corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda=-4.$" 13194139534670 17592186045417 true] [17592186124333 1074 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =-4.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]-(-4)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5{x}_{2}+8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $2$nd and the $3$rd). Thus, $x_1$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain $x_3=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get $x_2=0.$ \n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n![](images/cc/cca1254dd52432ccefc2cfe620c078494ae5f04f02f2f321beec36eef5ffb6fd.svg)\n\nTherefore, the required basis is\n![](images/bf/bfd00862d6d2d24221b11a4c5bf63baf21ab886cb1007b3164700d03eaf741bd.svg)" 13194139534670 17592186045417 true] [17592186124333 1074 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =-4.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]-(-4)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5{x}_{2}+8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $2$nd and the $3$rd). Thus, $x_1$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain $x_3=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get $x_2=0.$ \n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n![](images/43/4366abc9a1d46153708ef49ca06b25406739e06c5eaf3ee8c1a10c80081590f8.png)\n\nTherefore, the required basis is\n![](images/32/32cc18b0a63d50f6c20119cf7a437d7998123770320dcbfbe7e84f4833b2ff19.png)" 13194139534670 17592186045417 false] [17592186124334 1071 "![](images/8b/8be3045e233d200bb47b1cb936536b16090333f5633517b527fc2654ad72c1c1.svg)\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Find a basis of the eigenspace correspon